    "body": "Minimal implementation for \"Delayed Transaction Broadcast\" new feature.\r\n\r\nGoal: Allow a user to submit a transaction for delayed broadcasting, that will be broadcast only later, at a randomized time. The aim is increased privacy, by making time-correlation-based tracking more difficult.\r\nThis fits together with private broadcast: private connection broadcast tries to hide the originator node; randomized delay tries to hide the creation time.\r\n\r\nGoals in this PR: Extend the `sendrawtransaction` RPC with an optional `delay_for` parameter, and if set, postpone the initial broadcast to that later time, with some extra jitter.\r\n\r\nUse case Details, with the limitations of the current changeset:\r\n- What is a typical delay time? 30 - 90 minutes. (Too long times can get problematic: risk fee increase, node restart.)\r\n- Delayed broadcast is only supported with private broadcast.\r\n- Delay option and time is specified per submission (in `sendrawtransaction`). Alternative: with node level config.\r\n- For now pending transactions are NOT persisted, so pending transactions will be lost during a node stop/restart/crash.\r\n- Randomized delay is expressed as a percentage of the requested delay. A hard-coded value of 50% is used.\r\n- Delay times are capped: requested delay between 0min to 12 hours, randomization range to minimum 5 minutes.\r\n- Validation happens both at submission and broadcast time.\r\n- No special handling for sudden fee increase situations.\r\n- Pending (submitted but not yet submitted) transactions can be inspected via existing `getprivatebroadcastinfo` RPC.\r\n- The (pre-existing) `abortprivatebroadcast` RPC can be used to cancel a pending transaction submission.\r\n- No special `nLockTime` handling.\r\n- No special support from the wallet subsystem. (A submitted but not broadcast transactions is not visible in the wallet.)\r\n- No Undo/Cancel support at this time (to be added later).\r\n\r\nSolution Details:\r\n- The solution is based on the Private Broadcast implementation. \r\n- Transactions are stored in the already-existing `m_transactions` collection.\r\n- A scheduled periodic check is added to check for transactions that have became due. The implementation is very similar to the existing retry logic (`ReattemptPrivateBroadcast`).\r\n- Queue is not persisted currently.\r\n",
